Z||000000||Heisenhund||09-06-2000||08:03 PM||||In another thread ("Idle problems") I detail my problems in locating the cause of a high idle. When I disconnected the vacuum hose from the MAP sensor, Idle returned to normal. Replacing the sensor didn't work. In researching the sensor I came across an electrical print that shows the sensor getting 5V from the ECM. A quick check of that pin in the connector only shows about 1.5V on a 50 VDC scale. When I go to the next lower scale (2.5VDC) the meter pegs.<P>Could my refernce voltage from the ECM be bad? Any other way to check this? I checked the pther line to the TPS & got the same values.<P>Thanks,<BR>Heis<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||09-06-2000||11:03 PM||||Is the 50-volt scale really accurate down near zero volts?  Maybe you're really gettting 5 volts like it's supposed to be.<P>Not sure what kind of impedance your mechanical meter has.  If you can buy/borrow a high-impedance, digital voltmeter, you might get a better answer.     ||||reg||3
Z||000002||fierocrazy||09-06-2000||11:36 PM||||a MAP sensor would screw up all the time, I think I would check your vacuem first, I think it should be about 17 lbs at the plentuim<P>85GT 3.2||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||09-06-2000||11:37 PM||||Try another meter. You want a meter with a 20 volt scale. You can get a cheap digital meter at Wallmart and such. Most home stores have them as does radio shack.<P>Usually if the 5 volt supply is dead the whole ECM is done for. The same 5v feed runs multiple sensors. You could have just a bad line to the MAP but that's kind of unusual. If just that line is dead I'd question not just wires but the connector on the ECM.<P>Are you sure the vacuum line for the MAP sensor is connected to the right place on the engine end? Connecting it to the wrong port can make it do weird things.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Heisenhund||09-07-2000||07:46 AM||||Ogre it's attached to the inlet plenum right next to the sensor mounting bracket. A total run of about 2 inches of vacuum line. All hard line with the exception of the 2 rubber connectors, one to the plenum & one to the sensor.<P>???<BR>Heis<BR>(we need a smilie scratching his head!)||||reg||1
